\section{Lyapunov Stability Encoding}

Define the kernel Lyapunov functional:
\[
V_{\text{kernel}}(\Theta) = \Theta^\top P \Theta,
\]
with $P$ positive definite.

Lean~4 encoding:
\begin{verbatim}
def V (Θ : SKState) : Real :=
  dot Θ.toVector (P.mul Θ.toVector)

axiom P_posdef :
  forall x, x ≠ 0 -> dot x (P.mul x) > 0
\end{verbatim}

\section{Stability Criterion}

Autonomous stability requires:
\[
\frac{dV_{\text{kernel}}}{dt}
\le -\gamma \|\Theta\|^2 + C,
\]
with $\gamma > 0$ and bounded perturbation $C$.

Coq encoding:
\begin{verbatim}
Axiom dVdt_bound :
  forall Θ,
    dVdt Θ <= -γ * norm Θ^2 + C.
\end{verbatim}

\section{Main Stability Theorem}

\begin{theorem}[Global Autonomous Stability]
If $\gamma > 0$ dominates the perturbation bound $C$, then the SupraKernel
trajectory $\Theta(t)$ remains confined to a compact globally attractive
set $\mathcal{B}$.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Using $V_{\text{kernel}} \ge \lambda_{\min}(P)\|\Theta\|^2$, we obtain:
\[
\dot{V}_{\text{kernel}}
\le -\frac{\gamma}{\lambda_{\min}(P)} V_{\text{kernel}} + C.
\]
Applying Grönwall's inequality:
\[
V_{\text{kernel}}(t)
\le V_{\text{kernel}}(0)e^{-\alpha t}
+ \frac{C}{\alpha}(1 - e^{-\alpha t}),
\]
with $\alpha = \gamma/\lambda_{\min}(P)$.
Thus,
\[
\|\Theta(t)\|
\le \sqrt{\frac{C}{\alpha \lambda_{\min}(P)}},
\]
establishing global boundedness.
\end{proof}

Lean~4 theorem:
\begin{verbatim}
theorem SK_global_bound :
  exists B, forall Θ, V Θ <= C/α -> norm Θ <= sqrt (C/(α*λ_min)).
\end{verbatim}

